{{!--
	Advantage items whose `system.group` is not one of the four the sheet handles explicitly
	('', virtue, renown, quintessence). `prepareAdvantageLists` buckets them generically, so a splat can
	introduce a pool block purely as DATA — no code change — by giving its Advantage items a new group.

	add-wraith-pc-splat §3.2 — a heading was added here. Before, this partial rendered the items with no
	label at all, so a grouped block was visually separate but anonymous. Wraith needs the distinction to be
	legible, not merely present: Angst is the SHADOW's pool, it rises against the player, and a sheet that
	shows it as just another number beside Pathos invites it to be spent like one.

	The label chain mirrors the one `settings.hbs` already uses for the same data, so the two views of an
	Advantage group agree. An unrecognised group falls back to its raw name rather than rendering blank.

	Safe to change: measured 2026-07-31, no shipped data uses a group outside the four known ones, so this
	partial rendered nothing for any existing actor of any line.
--}}
{{#each groupedadvantages as |groupData|}}
	<div class="headlineGroup splatFont">
		{{#if (eq groupData.group "shadow")}}
			{{localize "wod.bio.wraith.shadow"}}
		{{else if (eq groupData.group "virtue")}}
			{{localize "wod.advantages.virtue.virtues"}}
		{{else if (eq groupData.group "renown")}}
			{{localize "wod.advantages.renown"}}
		{{else if (eq groupData.group "quintessence")}}
			{{localize "wod.advantages.quintessence"}}
		{{else}}
			{{groupData.group}}
		{{/if}}
	</div>

	{{#each groupData.items as |advantage id|}}
		<div class="sheet-boxcontainer">
			{{{getGetStatArea_v2 ../../actor advantage}}}
		</div>
	{{/each}}
{{/each}}
